Open questions
--------------

UNDETERMINED means the staged artifact carries no licence statement and none
was assumed. MITRE's CAPEC and CWE XML, the NIST OSCAL 800-53 catalog, the NIST
AI 100-2 and AI 600-1 PDFs, the NIST AI RMF, the AIUC-1 standard, and the OWASP
AI Exchange markdown all fall into this group. Each publisher states terms
somewhere outside the artifact this project downloaded. Resolving them means
recording the terms from the publisher's own page, not inferring them.

The OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications 2026 is pre-release. Its own revision
history still reads "[2026 release date]", so the artifact built from it pins
its version to the source sha256 rather than to a release date the publisher
has not set. Its licence block states CC BY-SA 4.0 and is recorded above as
such.

CSA's Cloud Controls Matrix and AI Controls Matrix both carry a notice
reserving redistribution. The project owner ruled on 2026-08-16 that CCM is
redistributable for this project's purposes, and CCM is therefore not in
RESTRICTED_FRAMEWORK_IDS. AICM was already tracked under the same terms. Both
are recorded here as the publisher states them.

The BASIS of the CCM ruling is not on record, and it must be. What is recorded
is that the owner ruled, not why. "We hold a written agreement with CSA",
"redistribution is covered by CSA membership" and "this is a fair-use judgment
about the quantity reproduced" are three materially different bases with three
different scopes, three different transferability properties for anyone forking
this repository, and three different answers to whether the same reasoning
reaches AICM. Until the basis is written down here, a downstream reader cannot
evaluate the ruling and cannot tell whether it applies to their use.

CSA's AI Controls Matrix (`csa_aicm`) is a live exposure, stated here without
being resolved. Measured on 2026-08-19: 243 controls tracked in git at
`data/processed/frameworks/csa_aicm.json`, description length 39 characters
minimum, 176 median, 485 maximum, which is control prose and not titles. Its
recorded notice is the same one CSA applies to CCM, reserving redistribution
outright. It appears in no licence tier: not in RESTRICTED_FRAMEWORK_IDS, not
in CONDITIONAL_FRAMEWORK_IDS, so not in OVERLAY_FRAMEWORK_IDS either. The
structural reason is that the tier derivation in
`tests/test_framework_licenses.py::_copyleft` selects on the substrings "GPL"
and "CC-BY-SA", so a publisher that reserves rights outright matches neither
and produces no tier membership at all. The model detects share-alike and is
blind to the stricter posture. This is a question for the project owner, and it
is a larger exposure than the copyleft frameworks the tiers were built for.


